File permissions
Command	Short detail
ls -l	                                                    Shows permissions, owner, group, size and modification time.
touch /home/atharv/atharvfile.txt	                                 Creates an empty file.
ls -ltr /home/atharv/atharvfile.txt	                             Displays the file in detailed time-sorted format.
touch testfile.txt	                                         Creates testfile.txt.
chmod 444 testfile.txt	                                     Sets read-only permissions for user, group and others.
chmod u+w testfile.txt	                                     Adds write permission for the owner.
chmod g+w,o+x testfile.txt	                                  Adds group write and others execute permissions.
ls -l testfile.txt	                                         Verifies the file permissions.
ls -l /home/testfile.txt	                                      Displays permissions/details of that file.
chown ashwini /home/atharv/atharvfile.txt	                       Changes file owner to ashwini.
chgrp soul /home/atharv/atharvfile.txt



practical 2:Password Aging

| useradd user2|                  Creates user `user2`. |
| passwd user2 |                        Sets password for `user2`. |
| chage -l user2 |                              Lists password-aging information for `user2`. |
| chage -m 1 -M 3 -W 1 -I 5 user2 |               Sets minimum age 1 day, maximum age 3 days, warning 1 day and inactive period 5 days. |
| chage -E 2026-09-20 user2 |                       Sets account expiration date to 20 September 2026. |
| chage -l user2 |                                 Verifies the changed password-aging settings. |

- -m → Minimum password age
- -M → Maximum password age
- -W → Warning days
- -I → Inactive days
- -E → Account expiration date


